    fix(web): expose corpus environment values in Submit form. Addresses DF-OFF-BY-ONE-54.
    
    The Submit form's environment select offered only Any/dev/staging/prod/
    ci/local, but the bundled corpus and API ship classes with environment
    "docker" and "linux" (internal/api tests already use both). Add the two
    options additively so the form's vocabulary covers the values the corpus
    carries. No wire change: the select still posts form-encoded/JSON the
    same way.
    
    The 409 dedup contract (re-submitting a class with a VERIFIED answer
    returns HTTP 409 with reason "answered" naming the existing solution,
    not a 200 queued response) is pinned by the existing
    TestSubmit_DedupVerifiedAnswer suite in internal/api; no API change was
    needed.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
---
 web/js/submit.js | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

